---
// How a Granite Guardian call works, in one picture.
---

<figure class="verdict" aria-label="A conversation plus a guardian block goes in; a yes or no verdict with a probability comes out">
  <div class="box">
    <span class="k">Input</span>
    <strong>The conversation</strong>
    <p>User turns, model turns, documents, tool calls.</p>
  </div>
  <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
  <div class="box guard">
    <span class="k">Guardian block</span>
    <strong>One criterion</strong>
    <p>Built in (harm, jailbreak, groundedness, tool-call validity) or written at runtime. Think or no-think.</p>
  </div>
  <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
  <div class="box out">
    <span class="k">Output</span>
    <strong><code>&lt;score&gt;yes&lt;/score&gt;</code></strong>
    <p>And the token probability behind it, as a continuous risk score.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

<style>
  .verdict {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .box {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
  }
  .box.guard {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .box.out {
    background: var(--accent-wash);
  }
  .k {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .box strong {
    display: block;
    margin: 4px 0 6px;
  }
  .box p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  .plus,
  .arrow {
    align-self: center;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .verdict {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .plus,
    .arrow {
      justify-self: center;
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }
  }
</style>
